  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ph 601.15 Prescription Labels",
  "priorExpiration": "2014-02-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ph 601.15 Prescription Labels.\n\n(a) Whenever an authorized practitioner dispenses a controlled drug, as defined in RSA 318-B:1-a and b, or a non-controlled prescription drug, as defined in RSA 318:1, XVII, he/she shall affix to the container in which such drug is dispensed, a label showing at least:\n\n(1) Name and address of the facility;\n\n(2) Name of the patient;\n\n(3) Date dispensed;\n\n(4) Name, strength and quantity of drug dispensed;\n\n(5) Directions for use;\n\n(6) Name of the prescribing practitioner;\n\n(7) Name or initials of the dispensing practitioner; and\n\n(8) All pertinent auxiliary labels.\n\nSource. #8572, eff 2-23-06, EXPIRED: 2-23-14\n\nNew. #12335, eff 7-22-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html"
